// The featured programs — guests with pre-written characters.
//
// Nine invitees arrive with a character sheet in their invitation. In
// the app they are ordinary guest programs: each is a bare CHARACTER
// (a name, a picture, at most a `wiki:` or a `wallet:` property), so it stays on the guest
// picker, can be captured, redeems codes, holds quests, answers
// choices, joins a faction and counts toward a majority.
//
// THE RULE: nothing anywhere in the story may make one of these a
// performer's part. No hooks, no beats, no `listed`, no `faction`, and
// no line anywhere that parses as their speech — a line that starts
// with one of these names and a colon is dialogue, and one dialogue
// line flips the program to a performer booth (identity.ts:isSpecial).
// Write their names as prose ("Microsoft Excel is Randy Barkmore Sr.").
//
// On arrival `ROLE Program` (main.loom) tags the guest by the exact
// picker spelling (`program.featured` = excel / openoffice / draftkings /
// bugdom / jeeves / runescape / mspaint / vlc / pong) and every later
// check reads that tag. Their private material comes from `The Uploader`
// and `Truther Download` lines and from `unlock`s gated on the tag.
// The human identities are in codex/5-people.loom; the real invitees'
// names never appear in the story.

CHARACTER Microsoft Excel
  avatar: File:Microsoft Office Excel (2013–2019).svg | File:Office Excel 2007 logo.svg

